'use client'

import { useEffect, useRef } from 'react'
import styles from './hero-field.module.css'

// Topographic contour-line field: decorative, animated hero background.
//
// 30 lines, built so they can never touch or cross: line[0] is a free-running
// "terrain" curve (a few low-frequency sine harmonics), and every line after
// it is line[i-1] + gap[i](x), where gap[i](x) = G(i) + a1*sin(...) + a2*sin(...)
// with a1+a2 kept strictly below G(i). Since sin() is bounded to [-1,1], that
// guarantees gap[i](x) >= G(i)-a1-a2 > 0 for every x by construction — not by
// checking samples after the fact.
//
// The spacing rule: G(i) = 25 + 10*sin(2π*i/7 + 0.6) + 4*sin(2π*i/11 + 2.4) —
// a function of the LINE INDEX i, not of x. A ~7-line cycle pulls a run of
// lines close together then eases them apart again, shaped by a slower
// ~11-line cycle so the rhythm doesn't repeat identically; both are smooth
// and continuous in i, so gaps change gradually rather than jumping straight
// from tight to wide. Real base_gap sequence this produces: 33,36,30,20,12,
// 12,20,31,38,36,27,19,16,21,27,31,28,22,17,18,26,35,38,32,22,13,12,19,29 —
// visibly tightening and loosening, never at random.
//
// Every frequency used is an integer multiple of 2π/W, so every line is
// exactly periodic: y(0) === y(W) to the decimal, meaning one tile's left and
// right edges match perfectly.
//
// Seamless-loop structure: .track is a flex row, 200% of .field's width, with
// two IDENTICAL tiles as its children (each flex-basis 50% of the track, i.e.
// exactly one .field-width). Animating .track by translateX(-50%) — one whole
// tile — at constant linear speed means the instant the animation wraps back
// to 0%, tile 2 sits exactly where tile 1 started. Invisible seam, constant
// speed throughout (no ease-in-out).

